  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe HTML spec states that the browser determines whether an element with `autofocus` attribute gets the focus during the [flush autofocus candidates process](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#flush-autofocus-candidates). For a custom element to be auto focused, at the time of flushing, it needs to be focusable, which means it needs to be defined already.\n\nThe flushing process happens either on the initial page load or when the element is added to the DOM after. Based on the current test results, seems when a custom element is upgraded, this process doesn’t run, and the spec doesn’t specify what to do when a custom element with `autofocus` attribute is upgraded.\n\nThis is a codepen with a few test cases to illustrate this issue: https://codepen.io/editor/marchbox/pen/019e9ab9-cd81-7c21-a3ae-1b7fe2d3458a",
